{"id":1800,"level":74,"name":"Підготовка відкритого нападу: шах","group":"Відкритий напад","format":27,"description":"<p>When performing a&nbsp;discovered attack, an important requirement is to set up a battery. Yet that itself is not sufficient. You also need to target enemy pieces. In the puzzles you've had to solve so far, those pieces to target were easy to find, but it's not always that simple. You sometimes have to do something extra for it, too! In the upcoming lessons you will have to play a preparatory move before you can successfully perform a discovered attack or discovered check. Here we distinguish between three types of forcing moves:</p>  <p>1) Check</p>  <p>2) Capture</p>  <p>3) Threat</p>  <p>A forcing move implies that you force the opponent to respond to your action:</p>  <p>If you give check, the other player must cancel the check. Their is no time&nbsp;to do anything else;</p>  <p>If you capture a piece, then the other player usually (sometimes it may be wise to do something else, but these cases are rare) captures the piece back. If you don't, you are a piece behind;</p>  <p>If you attack a piece, threaten to promote or mate, the other will often try to defend against this threat.</p>  <p>In this lesson you will learn to set up a battery by giving check. Then, by means of a discovered attack or discovered check, material can be gained. Fast forward to the example!</p>  <p><strong>What do you have to do?</strong><br />Set up a discovered attack by giving a check. Then win material by performing a discovered attack or discovered check.</p>","assignment":"","stickerID":72,"examples":[{"fen":"1k3B1r/1p6/pPp5/5b2/1P6/8/1KP5/4R3 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rb8,Gf8,Rh8] [#]} 1. Re8+ $1 Bc8 {[%csl Rb8,Rh8][%cal Ge8h8]} 2. Bd6+ Ka8 3. Rxh8 *","text":"<p>У нижньому ряду ми бачимо три фігури. Білі можуть поставити четверту фігуру в цьому ряду з перевіркою: 1.Re8+. Тепер білі не тільки націлюються на короля турою, але також біла тура опосередковано націлюється на чорну туру. Таким чином, білі налаштували батарею з темпом. Після 1...Bc8 білі можуть перевести ефективну відкритий напад в позицію 2.Bd6+. Білі виграють туру з другої чеки: 2...Ka8 3.Rxh8.</p>","format":27}],"puzzles":[{"id":75049,"fen":"6k1/5ppp/8/6Q1/1b6/3B3P/6PK/3q4 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rd1,Gd3,Gd8][%evp 0,5,718,734,756,759,775,775]} {[#]} {Q=1} 1. Qd8+ ! {[%csl Rd1,Gd3,Gd8]} Bf8 {Q=2} 2. Bxh7+ Kxh7 3. Qxd1 *","format":27,"texts":["Розглянемо форсування.","Використовуйте відкритий напад."],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":75062,"fen":"6k1/7p/1p3pnP/1Qb5/8/8/4B1PK/4q3 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Re1,Ge2,Ge8][%evp 0,5,1498,28178,29981,29982,29987,29988]} {[#]} {Q=1} 1. Qe8+ ! Nf8 {Q=2} 2. Bc4+ Kh8 3. Qxe1 *","format":27,"texts":["Розглянемо форсування.","Використовуйте відкритий напад."],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":75055,"fen":"1k1r4/1p6/1b3R2/4p3/8/1P1N4/PK6/8 b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Gd4,Ge5,Rf6][%evp 0,5,-183,-192,-190,-195,-215,-212]} {[#]} {Q=1} 1... Bd4+ ! (1... Rxd3? 2. Rxb6) (1... e4? 2. Rxb6) 2. Kc2 {Q=2} e4 3. Rf1 exd3+ *","format":27,"texts":["Розглянемо форсування.","Використовуйте відкритий напад."],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":75057,"fen":"7R/1kp4b/4r3/8/5N2/4nNPK/8/8 b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Gh6,Gh7,Rh8][%evp 0,5,-604,-633,-633,-633,-643,-645]} {[#]} {Q=1} 1... Rh6+ ! 2. Nh4 {Q=2} Bf5+ 3. Kh2 Rxh8 *","format":27,"texts":["Розглянемо форсування.","Використовуйте відкритий напад."],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":75053,"fen":"8/p4kp1/1p1n4/8/2P5/1r3B2/1P5P/1K1R4 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rb3,Gc4,Gd5][%evp 0,5,216,234,245,240,236,238]} {[#]} {Q=1} 1. Bd5+ ! Ke7 {Q=2} 2. c5 Re3 3. cxd6+ *","format":27,"texts":["Розглянемо форсування.","Використовуйте відкритий напад."],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":75056,"fen":"8/8/kp1N4/8/6p1/3R2P1/B5K1/q3b3 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Ra1,Ga2,Ga3][%evp 0,5,885,893,900,908,918,921]} {[#]} {Q=1} 1. Ra3+ ! Ba5 {Q=2} 2. Bc4+ Ka7 3. Rxa1 *","fo